  "description": "<div>\n  <p>An undirected tree on labels <code>1..n</code> has been given one extra edge. Remove the extra edge to restore a tree. If more than one listed edge could be removed, return the one latest in the input order.</p>\n  <p>The result preserves the selected edge’s endpoint order as written in the input.</p>\n  <p><strong>Example 1:</strong></p>\n  <pre><strong>Input:</strong> edges = [[1,2],[1,3],[2,3]]\n<strong>Output:</strong> [2,3]</pre>\n  <p>The final edge closes the triangle.</p>\n  <p><strong>Example 2:</strong></p>\n  <pre><strong>Input:</strong> edges = [[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[1,4],[1,5]]\n<strong>Output:</strong> [1,4]</pre>\n  <p>Joining 1 to 4 closes the four-node loop.</p>\n  <p><strong>Example 3:</strong></p>\n  <pre><strong>Input:</strong> edges = [[1,2],[2,3],[1,3]]\n<strong>Output:</strong> [1,3]</pre>\n  <p>Adding 1–3 makes a cycle.</p>\n  <p><strong>Constraints:</strong></p>\n  <ul>\n    <li><code>3 &lt;= n = edges.length &lt;= 100</code>.</li>\n    <li>Labels are distinct endpoints between <code>1</code> and <code>n</code>; no pair is repeated.</li>\n    <li>The graph was formed by adding exactly one edge to a tree.</li>\n  </ul>\n</div>",
